4. A price safety switch ships turned off and nothing in the
deployment turns it on
Path
src/Exchange.sol:173-187
Function Name
_skewOk
Description
Every swap combines two price readings: the price of gold, and the price of the stablecoin being traded.
Each is separately checked for freshness, and neither may be older than about 65 minutes.
But two readings can both be individually fresh and still come from very different moments. A gold price
from right now paired with a stablecoin price from 65 minutes ago passes both checks. The contract has
a setting to limit that gap.
That setting is missing from the deployment configuration, is never assigned at startup, and so defaults
to zero. Zero means "no limit, skip the check". No deployment script turns it on. The go live checklist
script, which verifies oracle health, reserves and compliance before opening trading, never checks it
either.
The code's own comment describes what is being left open: combining prices from different moments is
"an arbitrage/manipulation surface even when each feed independently passes its own freshness
